`chi.Walk` and `Router.Routes()` leave out a route that is registered on the same pattern as a `Route()` or `Mount()`. For example:

```go
r := chi.NewRouter()
r.Route("/foo", func(r chi.Router) {
    r.Route("/bar", func(r chi.Router) {
        r.Get("/{id}", handler)
    })
    r.Get("/bar", handler)
})
```

`GET /foo/bar` serves requests fine, but `chi.Walk(r, ...)` only reports `GET /foo/bar/{id}`, so docs generators built on it miss the endpoint.

Find the root cause and fix it. Walk and `Routes()` must report every routable endpoint, and must not start reporting anything they don't report today for routers without this collision. Add a regression test in the repo's style. `go test ./...` and `go vet ./...` must pass, and the code must be gofmt-clean.
